From e28e5c25fff81bb9a5ace3c28902872fa679e2f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:07:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net,http: log the OpenSSL in use, and test the hybrid key
 exchange

Nothing showed which OpenSSL a node runs, or whether its TLS client
offers the post-quantum hybrid group. The fallback to X25519 on
OpenSSL < 3.5 was silent, and no test checked the group our client and
server agree on.

- tls::HasHybridKeyExchange() reports whether X25519MLKEM768 is
  available (checked once). The client profile uses the same group lists.
- At HTTP server start the node logs, for example:
    Using OpenSSL 3.5.9 29 Sep 2026 (built with OpenSSL 3.5.9 29 Sep
    2026), TLS client key exchange X25519MLKEM768:X25519:P-256:P-384
- net_websocket_tests/tls_client_profile now checks that our client and
  server agree on TLS 1.3 and on X25519MLKEM768 from OpenSSL 3.5 on
  (X25519 before), and that HasHybridKeyExchange() matches the library
  version.
- PeerCertificate() drops its OpenSSL 1.1.1 branch, now that 3.0 is
  required.

Evidence (macOS arm64, depends' OpenSSL 3.5.9):
- test_bitcoin net_websocket_tests, httpserver_tests, net_tests and
  logging_event_tests: 73 cases, 3094 assertions pass (3 more than on
  the base tree).
- The TLS functional tests pass: p2p_websocket_*, interface_http_tls_certs,
  interface_http_publicbind, interface_http_public_fallback,
  interface_http_metrics, chronik_rpc_port_proxy and
  feature_p2p_privacy_recipes. rpc_bind skips on macOS as before.
- The log line above is from a p2p_websocket_tls.py node.

Not tested: the new assertions against OpenSSL 3.0-3.4. On 3.0/3.1 the
group-name check is compiled out (SSL_get0_group_name is 3.2+).

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Place runtime/default group policy after existing libevent removal; native Qt/ZMQ deletion preserves OpenSSL3.5 system/depends documentation.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
